# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vigilia Platform — Trivy CVE Ignore List
#
# Purpose: Document CVEs that have been consciously accepted.
#          Every entry MUST include a reason and a review date.
#          This file is auditable — do not add entries without team discussion.
#
# Format:
#   CVE-YYYY-XXXXX  # reason | review date
#
# Policy:
#   CRITICAL → must be resolved before merge (no ignore allowed)
#   HIGH     → must be resolved within 1 sprint (can be ignored with justification)
#   MEDIUM   → tracked but does not block pipeline
#   LOW      → ignored by default (not in Trivy severity filter)
#
# Note: prefer fixing via Dependabot PR over ignoring here.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Upstream transitive & base image vulnerabilities — reviewed & tracked for framework upgrade

# ── nginxinc/nginx-unprivileged:1.27-alpine OS packages ─────────────────────────
# Alpine base image packages — cannot be upgraded independently; tracked for next nginx-unprivileged release
CVE-2026-103111  # pcre2: Out-of-bounds write via crafted regular expression | review: 2026-12-15
CVE-2026-80145   # pcre2: PCRE2 out-of-bounds write allows arbitrary code execution | review: 2026-12-15
CVE-2026-80157   # pcre2: Out-of-bounds write via large pattern input | review: 2026-12-15
CVE-2026-80181   # pcre2: Memory corruption vulnerability in pcre2_jit_match | review: 2026-12-15
CVE-2026-4775    # tiff: libtiff arbitrary code execution or DoS via signed integer | review: 2026-12-15
CVE-2026-22184   # zlib: arbitrary code execution via buffer overflow in untgz utility | review: 2026-12-15

